Cross-corpus observation — 阴财神 appearing in two temples:
阴财神 is now documented at both Loyang Tua Pek Kong and Mun San Fook Tuck Chee. At Loyang she formed the material dimension of a three-bay eschatological programme alongside Dizang and 大二爷伯. At Mun San she appears as a peripheral entrance altar in a Tu Di Gong community temple with a specific annual 还库 ritual attached. The deity is consistent across both appearances; the institutional context differs substantially.
