Why Dou Mu surmounts the Tai Sui:
[DOU_MU  surmounts  CURRENT_YEAR_TAI_SUI]
  [scope: altar]

Theological claim:
  The Tai Sui system consists of 60 generals, one per
  year. The overall administrator of this system is
  Dou Mu — the cosmic mother-deity of the seven stars
  of the Big Dipper who governs all stellar fate.
  Placing her above the annual Tai Sui encodes the
  institutional hierarchy: individual annual fortune
  (Tai Sui) is governed by the comprehensive cosmic
  order (Dou Mu).

  Previously in this corpus, Tai Sui appeared at
  Loyang Tua Pek Kong beneath a Bodhisattva (Buddhist
  soteriological authority surmounting Taoist temporal
  administration). Here Tai Sui appears beneath Dou Mu
  (Taoist cosmic authority surmounting Taoist annual
  administration). Both configurations deploy the
  SURMOUNTS relation to encode hierarchical authority
  over the same deity class — through different
  traditional registers.
